# HTTP examples for module 13-reactive. Run them from IntelliJ IDEA / VS Code (REST Client).
# Start the lesson first: ./mvnw -pl modules/13-reactive/lesson spring-boot:run

### Functional endpoint + R2DBC
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books

### One book (404 if unknown)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/9780134685991

### Create a book
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780000000017", "title": "Reactive Spring", "price": 42.00}

### Add a review (reactive MongoDB)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books/9780134685991/reviews
Content-Type: application/json

{"author": "ada", "stars": 5, "text": "A classic."}

### Book + reviews from two databases (Mono.zip)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/9780134685991/details

### Live order feed (Server-Sent Events) — or: curl -N localhost:8080/api/orders/stream
GET http://localhost:8080/api/orders/stream
Accept: text/event-stream

### Place an order: every connected stream receives it
POST http://localhost:8080/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780134685991", "quantity": 2}
